.edu/documents/executive-order-11236-establishing-the-presidents-commission-law-enforcement-and"},"signing_date":null,"source_id":"app-executive-orders:EO:11236:common-crawl:86171625dd75","strong":false,"text_path":"../../app-executive-orders/output/texts/executive-order-11236-establishing-the-presidents-commission-law-enforcement-and.txt","why":"American Presidency Project (UCSB) web transcription: an editorial transcription published on the web, read live or from a web-archive capture of the page, NOT the signed or officially printed original; a lead to the original and to the text, never the original by itself"}],"savings_leads":[],"whole_order_end":[],"whole_order_end_total":0},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"research","counterevidence":"confirm","ending_or_current_basis":"research","opus_media":"research","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":["clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis","opus_media"],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1965-07-23","later-events_catalog":"1965-07-23","stage19_causal_queue":"1965-07-23"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:11236","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a ) There is hereby \nestablished the President’s Commission on Law  Enforcement and A d ­\nministration o f Justice (hereafter referred toids tho “ Commission” ).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b ) The Commission shall be composed of such members, not to \nexceed twenty, as the President shall appoint, one of whom shall be \ndesignated by the President as the chairman. The members and \nchairman of the Commission shall serve at the pleasure o f the \nPresident.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The President shall appoint an Executive Secretary, who shall \nreceive such compensation as the President shall specify. The func­\ntions and duties of the Executive Secretary shall be prescribed by the \nCommission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Functions of Commission. The Commission shall :","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(1) Inquire into the causes of crime and delinquency, measures for \ntheir prevention, the adequacy o f law enforcement and administration \no f justice, and the factors encouraging respect or disrespect for law, \nat the national, State, and local levels, and make such studies, conduct \nsuch hearings, and request such information as it deems appropriate \nfor this purpose.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 2(1)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec2(1)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(2) Develop standards and make recommendations for actions \nwhich can be taken by the Federal, State, and local governments, and \nby private persons and organizations, to prevent, reduce, and control \ncrime and increase respect for law, including, but not limited to, \nimprovements in training and qualifications o f personnel engaged in \nlaw enforcement and related activities, improvements in techniques, \norgauization, and administration o f law enforcement activities, im­\nprovements in the administration o f justice, improvements in correc­\ntion and rehabilitation of convicted offenders and juvenile delinquents, \npromotion o f better understanding between law enforcement officials \nand other members of the community, and promotion o f greater respect \nfor law throughout the community.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 2(2)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec2(2)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Executive Departments and Agencies; Judiciary.  The A t­\ntorney General, the Secretary of the Treasury, the Secretary of Health, \nEducation, and W elfare, and the Director o f the Office of Economic \nOpportunity each shall designate a representative to serve with the \nCommission as liaison. A ll executive departments and agencies shall \ncooperate with the Commission and furnish it such information and \nassistance, not inconsistent with law, as it may require in the per­\nformance o f its functions and duties. The Commission shall consult, \nas it deems appropriate, with members o f the Federal, State, and local \njudiciary and their assistants concerning matters of common interest.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 3","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Appointment of Committees.  The Chairman of the Com­\nmission, after consultation with the other members, and at such times \nas the Commission may deem appropriate, shall constitute Citizens \nAdvisory Committees (hereafter referred to as the “ Committees” )\n\n=== PDF page 6 of 88 ===\n9350 THE PRESIDENT\ncomposed o f persons (including persons from State and local govern­\nments and other public and voluntary organizations) who are authori­\nties in professional or technical fields related to crime or juvenile \ndelinquency, or persons representative of the general public who are \nleaders in activities concerned with crime or juvenile delinquency. \nThe Committees, and persons who are members, shall serve at the \npleasure o f the Commission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 4","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 5. Functions of Committees.  The Committees shall furnish \nthe Commission information, advice, and recommendations with re­\nspect to the functions set forth in section 2 o f this order and shall \nengage in such other activities as the Commission may deem \nappropriate.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 5","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec5","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. Compensation, Personnel, and Finance,","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 6 (lead-in)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec6","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a ) Members of \nthe Commission not otherwise employed by the United States shall \nreceive $100 per diem when engaged in the performance o f duties \npursuant to this order, and shall be allowed travel expenses and per \ndiem in lieu o f subsistence as authorized^ by law (5 U.S.C. 55a; 5 \nU.S.C. 73b-2) for persons employed intermittently.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 6(a)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec6(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b ) The Commission is authorized to appoint and fix the compensa­\ntion o f such other personnel as may be necessary to enable it to carry \nout its functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 6(b)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec6(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Commission is authorized to obtain services, including the \nservices o f individuals as members o f Committees, in accordance with \nthe provisions o f section 15 of the A ct of August 2, 1946 (5 U.S.C. \n55a), at rates for individuals not to exceed $100 per diem.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 6(c)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec6(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d ) A ll necessary expenses incurred in connection with the work \no f the Commission shall be paid from the “ Special Projects”  fund of \nthe President or such other appropriated funds as may be available \nfor the purposes of the Commission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 6(d)","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec6(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 7. Administrative Services.  The General Services Admin­\nistration shall provide administrative services for the Commission on \na reimbursable basis.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 7","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec7","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 8. Reports to the President and Termination.  The Commis­\nsion shall make reports and recommendations to the President from \ntime to time as it deems suitable and shall present a final report and \nrecommendations not later than eighteen months from the date of \nthis order. The Commission shall terminate not later than ninety \ndays after presenting such final report and recommendations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"30 FR 9349, PDF pages 5-10; Sec. 8","sha256":"dc1a6b12a510c471498adc4fa7f7b2494ce26699e223ddf809d06b165aaa4118","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1965-07-28/pdf/FR-1965-07-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11236#sec8","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"archival_id":"opus_stage11_evidence_originals:evidence/shards/S11_C_TEMP_X3/cache/fr_1965-07-28_p5-6.pdf","local_file_sha256":"77b8fbc31e3d57c718a0b376b50bb8779a98bc2f332ce71f2f75bf4f26126b18","page_or_item":"PDF pages 1-2 (heading on p1) of archived member evidence/shards/S11_C_TEMP_X3/cache/fr_1965-07-28_p5-6.pdf; Federal Register issue 1965-07-28 (file name)","sha256":"77b8fbc31e3d57c718a0b376b50bb8779a98bc2f332ce71f2f75bf4f26126b18"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 16 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:11236"}
